{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md && sed -n '1,190p' reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md && sha256sum AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean && sed -n '1,140p' aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md && sed -n '1,140p' aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\"","aggregated_output":"# P49 recovery review — finite-stage trace and compressed quasi-local corner\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: accepted after a provenance-only repair; queue may advance.**\n\nThe original fail-closed review remains preserved in\n`reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md`. It correctly halted P49 because\nthe packet and candidate declared `main.tex:1196-1335`, which omitted the\nfinite-stage vector-state and cyclicity clauses actually used by the module.\n\nThe source basis is corrected to `main.tex:1133-1261` in both\n`aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md` and the integrated\n`AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean`. This exact range contains:\n\n- vector fixing and normalization at lines 1133-1148;\n- the compressed vector functional and finite-stage cyclicity at lines\n  1150-1191;\n- the bounded strong-limit passage at lines 1193-1205; and\n- the norm-closure C-star extension at lines 1207-1261.\n\nLine 1262 begins the separate extension to the von Neumann corner, which is\ndeliberately excluded from P49 and remains the P50 gate. Thus the corrected\nlocator neither broadens the Lean theorem nor imports a downstream conclusion.\n\n## Artifact identity and scope preservation\n\nThe quarantined candidate had SHA-256\n`38d4cbb58104d88f9830aa6b73846d6309f497f48b4140f762a2f031343be487`.\nThe integrated candidate has SHA-256\n`12cc9185a24773f85855bfc05ee779e997bf40f05abb2823e3352932ffff7111`.\nAfter mechanically replacing only `main.tex:1196-1335` by\n`main.tex:1133-1261`, the sole remaining byte difference is one terminal blank\nline introduced by patch integration. No Lean declaration, theorem statement,\nproof term, import, assumption, or namespace was changed.\n\nThe corrected packet has SHA-256\n`251f2a0bec1737378f3c05b3d12fe61ad48a6588706f0b549bd973122ba62f95`.\nThe rejected closeout review is unchanged, with SHA-256\n`b62be4793f9cc195c87db9278eebec7bbac7a25d2f2f4d8bb839f43e0e13831d`.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The conditional finite-stage cyclicity, compressed vector functional, strong-limit vector identity, and norm-closed C-star traciality compile in the live Lean project. |\n| partial | This is not yet a normal or faithful trace on `q M_Gamma q`; those are P50 obligations. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the P49 gate after correcting its exact source locator. |\n| failed | None. The original failure was provenance-only and remains recorded in the rejected closeout. |\n\nAll auxiliary data remain explicit: finite-stage star representations,\nhermitian idempotent code projections, scalar-multiple normalized densities,\nthe vector-state identity, compatible inclusions, a decreasing projection\ntower, and a norm-density premise. No normality, faithfulness, finiteness,\nfullness, global weight, or type-III conclusion is asserted.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.FiniteCornerTrace AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower` — passed.\n- `lake env lean /tmp/P49AxiomAudit.lean` — passed; `finite_corner_trace`,\n  `stage_cyclic`, `tendsto_tauVec_sandwich`, and `CornerTracialOn.closure`\n  depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`; the temporary\n  audit file was removed afterward.\n- `lake build` — passed.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of P49 and its two plan predecessors —\n  no executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding remains. The correction was checked against the\ncanonical manuscript line by line. The theorem scope is still strictly below\nP50: it reaches only the norm-closed compressed quasi-local C-star algebra.\nCompilation does not establish the later normality, faithfulness, finiteness,\nfullness, or central type-III exclusion claims.\n\n## Supervisor recovery\n\nThe supervisor state may record this review as a manual, audited recovery while\nretaining the original closeout metadata as rejected history. P49 may be added\nto the accepted package set, which permits P50 to start because P49C has also\nbeen accepted. No remote result was cancelled or overwritten.\n\nAUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes\n\nAUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance\n# P50 recovery review — normal faithful corner trace\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: accepted after task-specific artifact recovery and a checked normality correction; queue may advance.**\n\nThe automated rerun closeout reviewed the package-level archive from the first\nrejected P50 task rather than the result of retry task\n`292ec9c3-b24f-40ea-958e-835d0bae4379`. The rejected closeouts remain preserved\nin `reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md` and\n`reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md`.\n\nThe actual retry project `d5eadb4d-3341-4f40-9129-85989734737e` was downloaded\nseparately to the ignored raw archive\n`aristotle_responses/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-rerun-d5eadb4d.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256 `72d1539f561204a4eaa28602c5759306ef2e973a3f1e2053c5fc3c69dde77e64`)\nand extracted without building or fetching dependencies into the task-specific\nquarantine directory `aristotle_responses/P50-rerun-d5eadb4d-quarantine/`.\nIts candidate `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` had SHA-256\n`cd61f079c7978bfb3bf5061e7b088522c7dc4620870cb9829df1dc44210e8a8d`.\n\nUnlike the stale first result, the actual retry defines the exported theorem\n`normal_faithful_corner_trace`, whose assumptions include P49's\n`CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem`, decreasing projection tower, and norm-density\ninput. It invokes `D.finite_corner_trace` directly and does not expose a supplied\n`CornerTracialOn`, bicommutant theorem, or Kaplansky-density interface.\n\n## Normality correction\n\nThe retry candidate originally stored only strong-operator continuity in the\nfield named `normal`. SOT continuity by itself is not the correct formal\nencoding of ultraweak normality. Before integration, the module was corrected\nto prove `cornerTau_continuous_wot`: the compressed vector functional is\ncontinuous for the weak operator topology. The `normal` field of\n`IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner` now stores this WOT-continuity theorem. This is\nstrong enough for the manuscript's normality claim because the functional is\nan ambient vector functional and every WOT-continuous linear functional is\nultraweakly continuous.\n\nThe final integrated candidate has SHA-256\n`2e9f93915721cf61978bd718ff972c3d0c26c8662efdc03fe7b91b65a627def2`.\nThe packet and candidate source basis is corrected to the exact manuscript\nrange `main.tex:1265-1417`, covering both the normal-trace and faithfulness\nproofs through the closing `\\end{proof}`.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe integrated module proves:\n\n- `cornerTau_continuous_wot`, plus strong-net and strong-partial-sum continuity;\n- `cornerTracialOn_bicommutant` and\n  `cornerTracialOn_vonNeumannGenerated`, using P49C's bounded compressed nets;\n- `cornerTau_faithful`, using traciality, the commuting complementary algebra,\n  and the dense span of vectors `b a Omega`;\n- `IsFaithfulNormalTracialCorner`, packaging projection membership,\n  normalization, positivity, traciality, WOT normality, and corner faithfulness;\n- `normal_faithful_corner_trace`, deriving C-star traciality from\n  `D.finite_corner_trace` and returning the packaged faithful normal finite\n  tracial state on the corner; and\n- `sanity_isFaithfulNormalTracialCorner`, showing the exported hypotheses are\n  jointly satisfiable.\n\nThe remaining explicit premises are the P49 finite codespace system, its\ndecreasing projection tower, a norm-closed represented star algebra containing\nthe finite stages and contained in their norm closure, a commuting\ncomplementary operator set, and density of the corresponding GNS vectors. No\nglobal trace or weight, fullness, projection finiteness, central-summand, or\ntype-III conclusion is assumed or asserted.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.NormalFaithfulCornerTrace` — passed.\n- `lake env lean /tmp/P50AxiomAudit.lean` — passed; the exported theorem,\n  WOT-continuity theorem, faithfulness theorem, and corner traciality theorem\n  depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`; the temporary\n  audit file was removed.\n- `lake build` — passed for the full live project.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan — no executable `sorry`, `admit`, user\n  `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration.\n- Source and theorem scan confirms the `main.tex:1265-1417` locator,\n  `D.finite_corner_trace` invocation, and WOT-valued `normal` field.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P50, Lane G — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P49 and P49C are accepted and compiled. The exported theorem\n  uses both rather than replacing either with a structure field.\n- **Gate:** faithful normal finite tracial state on the von Neumann corner —\n  discharged conditionally on the exact finite-system, represented-algebra,\n  complement-commutation, and dense-vector premises listed above.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. P51 still owns finiteness of `q`,\n  fullness, central finite projections, and type-III exclusion.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding remains. The review explicitly checked the\ntopology direction in the normality claim, the load-bearing P49 theorem call,\nthe P49C bounded-net use, the dense-set faithfulness route, and the separation\nfrom P51. Compilation does not discharge the remaining manuscript-specific\npremises; the theorem is conditional on them exactly as stated.\n\nAUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes\n\nAUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance\n12cc9185a24773f85855bfc05ee779e997bf40f05abb2823e3352932ffff7111  AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\n2e9f93915721cf61978bd718ff972c3d0c26c8662efdc03fe7b91b65a627def2  AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\ne57deb88999d442a8882f37fd4b956e7d36df5849b460dea9f5aa1c5bd1ddde4  AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\n# P49 — finite-stage trace and compressed quasi-local corner\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1133-1261`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P49`; Lane `G`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P47`, `P48`, both integrated and locally audited before submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** prove finite-stage cyclicity and its compatible compressed\n  quasi-local limit with finite codespace density data explicit.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no normality, faithfulness on the von Neumann\n  corner, fullness, global weight, or type-III exclusion.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean`. From the integrated\nprojection tower and explicit finite codespace density matrices, define the\nfinite-stage compressed functionals, prove compatibility and cyclicity, and\nconstruct the induced algebraic/continuous functional on the compressed\nquasi-local C-star algebra to the extent supported by the existing completion\ninterfaces.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nName every density, positivity, normalization, compatibility, boundedness, or\nC-star completion premise not derived in this module. Mark the theorem conditional.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean`; import P47 and P48\nplus the existing finite density/trace and algebraic inductive-limit modules.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.FiniteCornerTrace` succeeds without forbidden\ndeclarations. Report exact trace declarations, assumptions, and Plan alignment.\n# P50 — faithful normal tracial state on the von Neumann corner\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1265-1417`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P50`; Lane `G`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P49` and `P49C`, integrated and locally audited before submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** extend `tau_q` to `q M_Gamma q` and prove it is a\n  faithful normal finite tracial state under the exact required hypotheses.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no fullness, no statement about every central\n  summand, no global trace/weight, and no final type-III exclusion.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean`. Define the\ncorner functional induced by P49 in the represented von Neumann corner. Use the\nproved P49C bounded compressed approximants and bounded product convergence to\nprove cyclicity on all of `q M_Gamma q`. Prove positivity and unitality directly;\nprove normality from the vector-functional realization; and prove faithfulness\nfrom the manuscript's dense-vector/commuting-complement argument. The conclusion\nmust be a faithful normal finite **tracial state**, not merely a weight.\n\nThe exported P50 theorem must instantiate\n`CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace` from P49. Concretely, it\nmust take the compatible finite-codespace system, its decreasing projection\ntower, and the norm-density inclusion of the represented C-star algebra into\nthe closure of the finite-stage ranges, identify `q` with that tower's\n`limitProj`, and derive C-star-level `CornerTracialOn` by applying P49. An\ninternal abstract helper may accept a `CornerTracialOn` argument, but the main\nP50 conclusion may not expose `cstar_tracial` (or an equivalent cyclicity\nfield) as an auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList all representation, support, commutation, cyclicity-of-the-global-vector,\nand dense-vector premises explicitly; do not use a global trace. Bicommutant or\nKaplansky density may not remain as auxiliary assumptions because P49C proves them.\nThe norm-density premise required by P49 may remain explicit. Traciality or\ncyclicity of the compressed C-star functional may not remain explicit: it must\nbe derived from P49 in the exported theorem.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean`; import P49,\nP49C, and the checked C-star/GNS infrastructure as needed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.NormalFaithfulCornerTrace` succeeds without\nforbidden declarations. Positivity, normalization, traciality, normality, and\nfaithfulness must be proved under the explicit manuscript specialization data;\nthe response must name every remaining non-analytic premise. Acceptance also\nrequires a checked declaration whose assumptions include P49's finite-stage\nsystem and density input and do **not** include a supplied `CornerTracialOn`,\ntrace-cyclicity field, bicommutant theorem, or Kaplansky-density interface.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
